<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_8_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_8_2" name="8.2 Manage corrosion" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>Four of the six processes are drawn. 8.2.3 close interval survey and 8.2.5 internal corrosion are SPEC and are shown as the two places the flow leaves the cycle.

THE CLOSING EVENT IS A READING, NOT A SIGNATURE. 8.2.6 tracks the DEFICIENCY, and the flow returns to the reading to close it. Closing on the work order is how a deficiency disappears from the record while remaining in the ground, and it corrupts the 192.1007(e) programme measure at the same time.

49 CFR 192.465 carries the shortest recurring interval in the reference: (b) rectifiers six times each calendar year at intervals not exceeding 2.5 months. (a) sets 15 months for test station potentials, and (d) requires PROMPT remedial action without giving a figure - the figure is the operator's 192.605 manual, and that is what the tracking is measured against.

Gas only. There is no electric distribution corrosion regime because there is no federal electric distribution regime at all.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_8_2_lanes">
      <lane id="l_82_corr" name="Corrosion control">
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_which</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_rect</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_ts</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_atm</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_rec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_ok</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_esc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_cis</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_def</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_int</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_82_field" name="Field execution">
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_work</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_reread</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_82_cl</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_82_start" name="A corrosion monitoring reading falls due"><timerEventDefinition id="n_82_start_td"/></startEvent>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_82_which" name="Which monitoring obligation"/>
    <userTask id="n_82_rect" name="Read rectifier output"><documentation>8.2.1. 192.465(b): six times each calendar year at intervals not exceeding 2.5 months. The easiest interval in Subpart I to breach.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_82_ts" name="Read pipe-to-soil potential at the test station"><documentation>8.2.2. 192.465(a): at least once each calendar year at intervals not exceeding 15 months, against the criterion the operator adopted under 192.463.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_82_atm" name="Inspect exposed pipe for atmospheric corrosion"><documentation>8.2.4. 192.481, and (d) shortens the next interval where corrosion was found.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_82_rec" name="Record the reading with its method and criterion"><documentation>A reading without the criterion it was judged against cannot be re-evaluated.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_82_ok" name="Within the criterion"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_82_esc" name="Locating the deficiency needs more than a reading"/>
    <sendTask id="n_82_cis" name="Select a close interval survey"><documentation>8.2.3, SPEC. Part 192 neither requires nor defines it; AMPP SP0169 is the method and the trigger is the operator's.</documentation></sendTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_82_def" name="Open the deficiency and start its clock"><documentation>8.2.6. The DEFICIENCY is the tracked object, not the work order.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_82_work" name="Raise remedial work"><documentation>8.2.6. 192.465(d) requires prompt remedial action; 192.605 sets what prompt means.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_82_reread" name="Take the confirming reading"><documentation>8.2.6.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_82_cl" name="Deficiency corrected"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_82_int" name="Feed the finding to threat identification"><documentation>8.2.5 and 8.8.2. Internal corrosion found on removed pipe is a named threat input, not incidental history.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_82_end" name="Reading recorded, deficiency closed"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_start_n_82_which" sourceRef="n_82_start" targetRef="n_82_which" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_which_n_82_rect" sourceRef="n_82_which" targetRef="n_82_rect" name="rectifier or power source"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_which_n_82_ts" sourceRef="n_82_which" targetRef="n_82_ts" name="test station"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_which_n_82_atm" sourceRef="n_82_which" targetRef="n_82_atm" name="exposed pipe"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_rect_n_82_rec" sourceRef="n_82_rect" targetRef="n_82_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_ts_n_82_rec" sourceRef="n_82_ts" targetRef="n_82_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_atm_n_82_rec" sourceRef="n_82_atm" targetRef="n_82_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_rec_n_82_ok" sourceRef="n_82_rec" targetRef="n_82_ok" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_ok_n_82_int" sourceRef="n_82_ok" targetRef="n_82_int" name="within criterion"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_ok_n_82_esc" sourceRef="n_82_ok" targetRef="n_82_esc" name="deficiency"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[withinCriterion = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_esc_n_82_cis" sourceRef="n_82_esc" targetRef="n_82_cis" name="cannot be located from readings"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_cis_n_82_def" sourceRef="n_82_cis" targetRef="n_82_def" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_esc_n_82_def" sourceRef="n_82_esc" targetRef="n_82_def" name="located"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_def_n_82_work" sourceRef="n_82_def" targetRef="n_82_work" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_work_n_82_reread" sourceRef="n_82_work" targetRef="n_82_reread" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_reread_n_82_cl" sourceRef="n_82_reread" targetRef="n_82_cl" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_cl_n_82_work" sourceRef="n_82_cl" targetRef="n_82_work" name="not yet corrected"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[corrected = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_cl_n_82_int" sourceRef="n_82_cl" targetRef="n_82_int" name="corrected"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_82_int_n_82_end" sourceRef="n_82_int" targetRef="n_82_end" name=""/>
  </process>
